      <h1 id="oadp-use-case-enable-ca-cert" class="group scroll-mt-20">Including a self-signed CA certificate during backup<a href="#oadp-use-case-enable-ca-cert" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p>You can include a self-signed Certificate Authority (CA) certificate in the Data Protection Application (DPA) and then back up an application. You store the backup in a NooBaa bucket provided by Red Hat OpenShift Data Foundation (ODF).</p>
      <h2 id="oadp-usecase-include-ca-cert-backup_oadp-use-case-enable-ca-cert" class="group scroll-mt-20">Backing up an application and its self-signed CA certificate<a href="#oadp-usecase-include-ca-cert-backup_oadp-use-case-enable-ca-cert" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">The <code>s3.openshift-storage.svc</code> service, provided by ODF, uses a Transport Layer Security protocol (TLS) certificate that is signed with the self-signed service CA.</p>
      <p>To prevent a <code>certificate signed by unknown authority</code> error, you must include a self-signed CA certificate in the backup storage location (BSL) section of <code>DataProtectionApplication</code> custom resource (CR). For this situation, you must complete the following tasks:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>Request a NooBaa bucket by creating an object bucket claim (OBC).</li>
      <li>Extract the bucket details.</li>
      <li>Include a self-signed CA certificate in the <code>DataProtectionApplication</code> CR.</li>
      <li>Back up an application.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You installed the OADP Operator.</li>
      <li>You installed the ODF Operator.</li>
      <li>You have an application with a database running in a separate namespace.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Create an OBC manifest to request a NooBaa bucket as shown in the following example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: objectbucket.io/v1alpha1\nkind: ObjectBucketClaim\nmetadata:\n  name: test-obc\n  namespace: openshift-adp\nspec:\n  storageClassName: openshift-storage.noobaa.io\n  generateBucketName: test-backup-bucket"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>test-obc</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the name of the object bucket claim.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>test-backup-bucket</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the name of the bucket.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the OBC by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create -f <obc_file_name>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      When you create an OBC, ODF creates a <code>secret</code> and a <code>ConfigMap</code> with the same name as the object bucket claim. The <code>secret</code> object contains the bucket credentials, and the <code>ConfigMap</code> object contains information to access the bucket. To get the bucket name and bucket host from the generated config map, run the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc extract --to=- cm/test-obc"} lang="terminal" />
      <p><code>test-obc</code> is the name of the OBC.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"# BUCKET_NAME\nbackup-c20...41fd\n# BUCKET_PORT\n443\n# BUCKET_REGION\n\n# BUCKET_SUBREGION\n\n# BUCKET_HOST\ns3.openshift-storage.svc"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      To get the bucket credentials from the <code>secret</code> object, run the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc extract --to=- secret/test-obc"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID\nebYR....xLNMc\n# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\nYXf...+NaCkdyC3QPym"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Create a <code>cloud-credentials</code> file with the object bucket credentials by using the following example configuration:
      <CodeBlock code={"[default]\naws_access_key_id=<AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID>\naws_secret_access_key=<AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the <code>cloud-credentials</code> secret with the <code>cloud-credentials</code> file content by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create secret generic \\\n  cloud-credentials \\\n  -n openshift-adp \\\n  --from-file cloud=cloud-credentials"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Extract the service CA certificate from the <code>openshift-service-ca.crt</code> config map by running the following command. Ensure that you encode the certificate in <code>Base64</code> format and note the value to use in the next step.
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get cm/openshift-service-ca.crt \\\n  -o jsonpath='{.data.service-ca\\.crt}' | base64 -w0; echo"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"LS0tLS1CRUdJTiBDRVJUSUZJQ0FURS0...\n....gpwOHMwaG9CRmk5a3....FLS0tLS0K"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Configure the <code>DataProtectionApplication</code> CR manifest file with the bucket name and CA certificate as shown in the following example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: oadp.openshift.io/v1alpha1\nkind: DataProtectionApplication\nmetadata:\n  name: oadp-backup\n  namespace: openshift-adp\nspec:\n  configuration:\n    nodeAgent:\n      enable: true\n      uploaderType: kopia\n    velero:\n      defaultPlugins:\n        - aws\n        - openshift\n        - csi\n      defaultSnapshotMoveData: true\n  backupLocations:\n    - velero:\n        config:\n          profile: \"default\"\n          region: noobaa\n          s3Url: https://s3.openshift-storage.svc\n          s3ForcePathStyle: \"true\"\n          insecureSkipTLSVerify: \"false\"\n        provider: aws\n        default: true\n        credential:\n          key: cloud\n          name:  cloud-credentials\n        objectStorage:\n          bucket: <bucket_name>\n          prefix: oadp\n          caCert: <ca_cert>"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>insecureSkipTLSVerify</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies whether SSL/TLS security is enabled. If set to <code>true</code>, SSL/TLS security is disabled. If set to <code>false</code>, SSL/TLS security is enabled.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;bucket_name&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the name of the bucket extracted in an earlier step.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;ca_cert&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the <code>Base64</code> encoded certificate from the previous step.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the <code>DataProtectionApplication</code> CR by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc apply -f <dpa_filename>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Verify that the <code>DataProtectionApplication</code> CR is created successfully by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get dpa -o yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: v1\nitems:\n- apiVersion: oadp.openshift.io/v1alpha1\n  kind: DataProtectionApplication\n  metadata:\n    namespace: openshift-adp\n    #...#\n  spec:\n    backupLocations:\n    - velero:\n        config:\n          #...#\n  status:\n    conditions:\n    - lastTransitionTime: \"20....9:54:02Z\"\n      message: Reconcile complete\n      reason: Complete\n      status: \"True\"\n      type: Reconciled\nkind: List\nmetadata:\n  resourceVersion: \"\""} lang="yaml" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Verify that the backup storage location (BSL) is available by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get backupstoragelocations.velero.io -n openshift-adp"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME           PHASE       LAST VALIDATED   AGE   DEFAULT\ndpa-sample-1   Available   3s               15s   true"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Configure the <code>Backup</code> CR by using the following example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: velero.io/v1\nkind: Backup\nmetadata:\n  name: test-backup\n  namespace: openshift-adp\nspec:\n  includedNamespaces:\n  - <application_namespace>"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;application_namespace&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the namespace for the application to back up.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the <code>Backup</code> CR by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc apply -f <backup_cr_filename>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Verify that the <code>Backup</code> object is in the <code>Completed</code> phase by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc describe backup test-backup -n openshift-adp"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"Name:         test-backup\nNamespace:    openshift-adp\n# ....#\nStatus:\n  Backup Item Operations Attempted:  1\n  Backup Item Operations Completed:  1\n  Completion Timestamp:              2024-09-25T10:17:01Z\n  Expiration:                        2024-10-25T10:16:31Z\n  Format Version:                    1.1.0\n  Hook Status:\n  Phase:  Completed\n  Progress:\n    Items Backed Up:  34\n    Total Items:      34\n  Start Timestamp:    2024-09-25T10:16:31Z\n  Version:            1\nEvents:               <none>"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      </ul>
